# Build context for the production image (P10-1, Dockerfile at this level).
#
# The context is the whole repo because the image builds the frontend itself
# (see Dockerfile). Without this file the daemon would ship ~1 GB of
# node_modules/.venv/.git before the first instruction runs, and any stray file
# under them would bust every layer cache.
#
# Note: compose.dev.yml builds backend/Dockerfile.dev with context ../backend,
# and a .dockerignore is resolved against the CONTEXT root — this file does not
# apply there. That build is unchanged and out of scope here.

# Dependency + build output trees (both are rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/.venv
frontend/dist
frontend/.angular
backend/widget_dist
backend/studio_dist

# Python/test/lint caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Test + report artefacts
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report
evals/reports

# evals/ MUSS im Kontext bleiben: die Gold-FLOWS liegen zwar im Config-Store,
# aber die Runner-DATEI evals/run_golden.py lädt das Backend zur LAUFZEIT per
# Pfad (EVAL_RUNNER_PATH), und das Dockerfile kopiert genau sie ins Image.
# Ein pauschales `evals` hier ließ den COPY mit „not found" scheitern
# (CI-Befund 2026-08-22); reports/ ist oben ausgeschlossen, __pycache__ global.
docs
.github
.git
.gitignore
CLAUDE.md

# Lokale Rückfall-Kopien des Seed-Baums (F0): gehören nicht ins Image und
# würden bei jeder neuen Sicherung den Layer-Cache brechen.
backups

# Secrets never enter an image layer (they would survive in the history even if
# a later layer deleted them).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
